title: "Everyone Reads Your Permission Generously"
description: "Fourteen years of fighting over §1033 covered basic bank accounts and credit cards. The access you actually grant has no declared scope and no committed duration."
subtitle: "Consumer financial data moves constantly. Everyone sets the terms except the person it belongs to."
slug: everyone-reads-your-permission-generously
date: 2026-08-04
author: Vevina McAllister
eyebrow: Open Banking
tags: [open banking, CFPB 1033, bank data, data portability, fintech, consumer data rights, aggregators, Plaid]
draft: false
hero: /blog/everyone-reads-your-permission-generously/pointing.jpg
og_image_alt: "Figures in overcoats and fedoras stand in a circle outside a neoclassical bank, each pointing at someone else. The facade reads: Institutions write the rules, everyone reads them generously."

